1
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,040
I can say it with certainty.

2
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:12,680
In this entire world, no one is as hated by digital devices as I am.

3
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:17,040
If I touch a computer, I hit a bug.

4
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:18,880
If I touch a smartphone, it freezes.

5
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:23,360
Virus infections? All the time.

6
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:33,600
But I believe that someday, we'll be able to get along.

7
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,800
So please... just let today be the day.

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:56,482
Why does this always happen to me!?

9
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:29,680
Understand?

10
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,840
What we must aim for is perfection.

11
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:36,160
I want each and every one of you to be aware that you are the ones supporting this railway.

12
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:44,360
Safety and security are the keys to earning our passengers' trust.

13
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:47,600
As I've said many times: zero computer virus infections!

14
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,280
Zero information security incidents!

15
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:53,480
That should be a given!

16
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:56,080
And yet you can't even manage that!

17
00:02:57,080 --> 00:03:00,040
Anyone who gets infected is just as guilty as the hacker!

18
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:03,720
Disciplinary action will be unavoidable, of course.

19
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:08,560
I heard someone in the International Division got demoted.

20
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:11,320
You'd better be especially careful, Mei...

21
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:16,545
Unfortunately, that concern is well-founded.

22
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:22,440
I'm next. That's what I thought.
(Katsuragi) Be aware of your duty as railway employees and devote yourselves to your work.

23
00:03:24,133 --> 00:03:29,162
Awareness -- right, I need to be more aware.

24
00:03:30,373 --> 00:03:32,813
Understand?

25
00:03:32,853 --> 00:03:35,613
I won't get infected by viruses anymore!

26
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:41,453
Uuugh... my computer is acting weird.

27
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,040
She just said that and already...

28
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,600
We need to contact the System Division...

29
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:52,920
We'll get fired -- both you and me...

30
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,824
Um, Uyagawa, I'm sorry!

31
00:03:54,849 --> 00:03:57,680
Could you please keep this between us?

32
00:03:58,145 --> 00:04:00,530
Sure, no problem.

33
00:04:00,555 --> 00:04:03,635
Just be more careful from now on, okay?

34
00:04:06,089 --> 00:04:08,975
I've removed the virus.

35
00:04:09,211 --> 00:04:11,840
Thank you so much!

36
00:04:12,039 --> 00:04:14,930
Saved by the skin of my teeth...

37
00:04:15,055 --> 00:04:17,735
Director Katsuragi isn't kidding around, you know.

38
00:04:17,778 --> 00:04:21,844
You really need to be more aware
and stop causing trouble for other people.

39
00:04:21,999 --> 00:04:23,639
Yes...

40
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:29,619
Ugh... of all days, today is just not my day...

41
00:04:30,062 --> 00:04:33,782
Sorry, Agaho, can you get the phone?

42
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:39,040
Thank you for calling.

43
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:41,554
Kyoki Railway PR Department, Agaho speaking.

44
00:04:41,604 --> 00:04:43,483
(Phone voice) My name is Asagiri Yoshimitsu.

45
00:04:44,216 --> 00:04:47,657
You see, starting a few minutes ago, on our website...

46
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:52,273
We've been receiving suspicious traffic resembling a DoS attack from your IP address.

47
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:56,028
Huh!?

48
00:04:56,395 --> 00:05:01,680
IP...?
DoS...koi?

49
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,462
It was a prank call!

50
00:05:07,706 --> 00:05:10,128
Ah-- hey, wait!?

51
00:05:10,861 --> 00:05:14,160
There sure are a lot of weirdos out there.

52
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:17,239
Well, at least that was a change of pace.

53
00:05:17,617 --> 00:05:19,840
(Colleague) The Kobe TV crew is here.

54
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:22,240
Coming!

55
00:06:55,520 --> 00:07:00,160
Is it just me, or is Tarumi not here again?

56
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,800
Don't worry, that's her hobby.

57
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:08,000
I think she's driving a train -- a special service.

58
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,600
Basically a hobby.

59
00:07:10,271 --> 00:07:11,551
Doors closed, check!

60
00:07:11,576 --> 00:07:13,016
Side lights, check!

61
00:07:13,041 --> 00:07:15,441
Platform, check!

62
00:07:15,466 --> 00:07:18,026
Departure equivalent -- proceed!

63
00:07:25,812 --> 00:07:27,892
I knew it was Akane!

64
00:07:27,959 --> 00:07:29,959
We're not using anything that heavy!

65
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,160
Hello, this is Hosono from the System Division.

66
00:07:33,706 --> 00:07:35,786
We've been getting nonstop alerts since this morning.

67
00:07:36,399 --> 00:07:41,346
Main Line -- 431M, 441M, 2103D!

68
00:07:41,612 --> 00:07:43,840
At 9:35, upon request from National Railways--

69
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,960
Emergency broadcast!

70
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,740
Multiple signals passed at danger!

71
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:51,920
Whaaaat!? I didn't do anything!?
